------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / PARITY (web source reproduced verbatim — no narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web SubscribeCard is a pure presentational alert-channel discoverability tile (no query/hook): a
bell header "Get notified about incidents", the self-hosted explainer line, and a grid-cols-1
sm:grid-cols-2 grid of five <ChannelTile> rows linking to the channel setups. Every literal + structure
is reproduced:
  • Header  : SF "bell" + t(subscribe.title, "Get notified about incidents")
  • Caption : t(subscribe.description, "Self-hosted: configure your own channels for status events.")
  • Tiles   (web order, lucide→SF, web `to` preserved):
      Email       Mail→envelope                          "SMTP-based delivery"      /notifications/channels
      Slack       MessageSquare→message                  "Webhook channel"          /notifications/channels
      Discord     Hash→number                            "Webhook channel"          /notifications/channels
      Webhook     Webhook→point.3.connected.trianglepath "Custom HTTP endpoint"     /notifications/channels
      Browser push Smartphone→iphone                     "Opt-in PWA notifications" /settings/notifications
  • Grid    : LazyVGrid adaptive(min 240) → 1 column compact, 2 across regular (web sm:grid-cols-2)

Architecture follows the accepted presentational-nav precedent QuickNavWidget(0075) + ResultPanel(0008)
+ AiUsageCard(0237): the surface is NOT a bare static view — it honours the leaf contract through a
P1/S8 state-holder seam so every state renders and previews/tests drive them:
  • P1/S8  state-holder : SubscribeCardSource protocol; SubscribeCardModel(@Observable, @MainActor);
                          StaticSubscribeCardSource (production, publishes the static catalog, .live);
                          InMemorySubscribeCardSource (preview/test). No HTTP / no navigation in the view.
  • P1/S9  tokens       : Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius only — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex.
  • P1/S10 i18n         : SubscribeCardStrings facade (.string/.text/.format), per-surface "SubscribeCard"
                          table; 24 keys, English fallbacks promoted from the web literals (no Swift prose).
  • P1/S11 telemetry    : view.opened surface="SubscribeCard" emitted once on first start.
  • Navigation          : onNavigate:((String)->Void)? — host resolves the deep link (web <Link to>).
  • States (all render) : loading (skeleton grid) / empty (friendly, never blank) / error (retry) /
                          content (the 5-tile grid); ORTHOGONAL connection axis live/stale/offline →
                          header freshness chip + banner above the grid + one-shot stale auto-refresh.
  • A11y                : each tile is a Button w/ VoiceOver label ("<label>. <desc>") + hint ("Opens X");
                          header isHeader trait; Dynamic-Type tokens; reduce-motion-aware press feedback.

